16. Match lifecycle and deterministic behaviour

All structural damage and weather state must belong to an individual Arena instance.

On a new battle:

* Both side sections are fully intact.
* Both counters are zero.
* The centre is untouched.
* No collapse debris remains.
* The weather controller starts fresh.
* The initial weather is calm.

On a rematch, fully reset the Jökull stage.

On an ordinary fighter respawn within the same match, do not reset the stage.

Destroyed sections must remain destroyed.

Damage counters must persist through individual eliminations and respawns.

Where appropriate, match freeze, result-screen and restart behaviour should follow the established hazard lifecycle.

Random weather decisions must use dedicated seeded streams and be reproducible for the same battle seed and gameplay update sequence.

The actual weather sequence must not change because the user resizes the screen or because the game renders at a different frame rate.

